 "post": {
  "title": "The Reverse of Stockholm Syndrome #shorts",
  "description": "Rosa's job is to keep Milo and June locked in an escape room for an hour. Thirty minutes in, she opens the door. Stockholm syndrome is hostages bonding with their captors; Lima syndrome is the reverse: captors growing attached to the people they hold. It is named after the Japanese embassy hostage crisis in Lima, Peru, which began on 17 December 1996, when MRTA rebels took more than 600 people hostage at the Japanese ambassador's residence. Within weeks hundreds were released, and some of the young captors were reported to have grown attached to their hostages. Honest caveat: the term comes from that one famous case and a few anecdotes, not from controlled studies. #psychology #shorts #limasyndrome #stockholmsyndrome",
